  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NGA_ACJR2024 (Joint Budget)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMMARY
The Dutch Relief Alliance has activated its fastest crisis response mechanism to develop an emergency humanitarian response within 72-hours to assist flood-affected populations in North-East Nigeria (Borno State). Six Dutch based NGOs (Plan International, Oxfam, CARE, Terre des Hommes, ZOA &amp; Stichting Vluchteling/IRC) together with seven local NGOs (CHAD, CRUDAN, CATAI, CBI, EYN, LABDI, LHI &amp; GHV Africa) have joined hands to provide emergency relief including access to safe drinking water, in order to prevent illnesses like cholera, providing food and financial assistance to replace belongings lost during the floods, as well as emergency protection services such as assisting children who have lost their families. At least 130.000 people will be supported with such assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
